  "title": "The knot's three-fold spaces are the triple systems that resist 2-colouring",
  "subject": "Gluings of triangles whose contacts all join three triangles, and the signed not-all-equal knot at its angle",
  "conclusion": "Such a gluing is a space for the knot exactly when its dual triple system resists 2-colouring but stops resisting once the corner line is removed, which is the classical even-cycle problem whose one indecomposable exception is the Fano plane. Up to 13 triangles only the Fano plane and its splice occur, and Fano planes splice together without limit.",
